{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Cubemap"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritsFrom","title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ImageTextureLayered"]},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SQ","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SH","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s12IdentifiableP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VariantConvertible"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Cubemap","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Cubemap","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Cubemap"}],"externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot7CubemapC","symbolKind":"class","roleHeading":"Class"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Cubemap\/createPlaceholder()"],"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Cubemap\/godotClassName"],"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/cubemap"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Cubemap"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A cubemap is made of 6 textures organized in layers. They are typically used for faking reflections in 3D rendering (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). It can be used to make an object look as if it’s reflecting its surroundings. This usually delivers much better performance than other reflection methods."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This resource is typically used as a uniform in custom shaders. Few core Godot methods make use of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Cubemap","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" resources."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To create such a texture file yourself, reimport your image files using the Godot Editor import presets. To create a Cubemap from code, use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ImageTextureLayered\/createFromImages(_:)"},{"text":" on an instance of the Cubemap class.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The expected image order is X+, X-, Y+, Y-, Z+, Z- (in Godot’s coordinate system, so Y+ is “up” and Z- is “forward”). You can use one of the following templates as a base:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2×3 cubemap template (default layout option)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"3×2 cubemap template"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"1×6 cubemap template","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"6×1 cubemap template"}]}]}]},{"name":"Note","style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Godot doesn’t support using cubemaps in a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/PanoramaSkyMaterial","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". To use a cubemap as a skybox, convert the default ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/PanoramaSkyMaterial","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ShaderMaterial","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" using the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Convert to ShaderMaterial","type":"text"}]},{"text":" resource dropdown option, then replace its code with the following:","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After replacing the shader code and saving, specify the imported Cubemap resource in the Shader Parameters section of the ShaderMaterial in the inspector."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Alternatively, you can use ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"this tool"},{"type":"text","text":" to convert a cubemap to an equirectangular sky map and use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/PanoramaSkyMaterial","isActive":true},{"text":" as usual.","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Six square textures representing the faces of a cube. Commonly used as a skybox."}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/SH":{"title":"Swift.Hashable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SH"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Image/create(width:height:useMipmaps:format:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/image\/create(width:height:usemipmaps:format:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"create","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"width"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5Int32V","text":"Int32"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"height",